let's face it we are creative beings  designed to imagine and create from the  moment we arrive to this world  but somewhere along our lives we are  told to stop dreaming stop building or  tearing things apart to face reality and  get a real paying job and we lose our  creativity we go from thinking we could  be the first astronaut on mars  to feeling stuck in the hamster wheel  and end up feeling burnt out  unproductive and unmotivated  but creativity is key to our success and  happiness  you see if we were made in the image and  likeness of a creator  we are born to create  creative thinking has led to unique  designs that inspire inventions that  help improve our lives and it can change  your life  your creative energy is waiting to be  unleashed so whether or not you're  feeling stuck in an unmotivated rut  you're feeling burnt out or unproductive  or you just need some inspiration for  your creative projects i hope that this  video will be helpful for you if you  like this video please give it a thumbs  up and help support my channel but if  not by all means give it a thumbs down  but please give me some feedback in the  comments so that i know what to work on  all right let's get started number one  is to limit media consumption the first  and foremost thing that i have to say  before trying any of the other tips is  to stop that dopamine spike through  media consumption take a social media  fast stop using your phone or scrolling  through instagram the first thing you do  in the morning do yourself a favor and  stop watching the news my husband and i  recently took a trip to gatlinburg  tennessee to celebrate our anniversary  and the hotel there had the news on  every single morning at the breakfast  area we haven't had a tv in years but it  was a great reminder of why we do not  miss it because how is being reminded  that there is evil in the world supposed  to encourage and uplift my mood or how  am i supposed to feel creative and  motivated when the news or just media in  general is constantly reminding me of  all the things that could go wrong all  the people that are doing it better than  me or that i should just plain lose hope  and humanity because humans are evil  stop watching the news limit all media  as much as possible and make sure that  the media that you are consuming is  positive in nature this will make it so  that everything else that i mentioned in  this video will be much more effective  in helping you spark your creativity  number two is to write down 10 ideas  daily i started to do this about two  years ago inspired by the author james  altucher who writes in his book choose  yourself  the way you get good ideas is to do two  things  one  read two hours a day  two  write ten ideas a day  by the end of the year you will have  read for almost one thousand hours and  write down three thousand 600 ideas  one of these will be a home run  when i first began to implement this i  admit in the beginning it was not only  difficult but it felt kind of silly and  it was actually something that would  take me a while i'd sit there and think  i don't i don't know ideas about what  and it took me a while to actually start  thinking of ideas but i found that the  more i did it every single day the more  ideas i had and then pretty soon it not  only meant that i had the 10 ideas per  day i had more ideas the ideas can be  something really simple like change that  light bulb in the bathroom that you've  been meaning to do but you've been  procrastinating on or it can be  something big like for me doing a live  stream someday or having a podcast if  those ideas don't actually come to  fruition what you're doing by writing  them down is giving those ideas a place  to land so that you can actually act  towards them and possibly achieve them  doing this consistently has definitely  changed my life number two is also one  that i really love is morning pages and  this one is inspired by the author julia  cameron i've read several of her books  she is amazing but i highly recommend  the artist's way because she allowed me  to think of creativity as something that  is necessary rather than something that  i need to just push aside because i need  to be an adult and get things done but  the concept of morning pages is kind of  like a brain dump the first thing that  you do in the morning is get out a pen  and paper or a notebook or journal  whatever it is that you want to write on  and just write down whatever comes to  mind without worrying about grammar or  what your writing looks like you're just  going to write down anything that's on  your mind and the point of this is  really to bring to the surface anything  that's been bothering you and expand  upon it or expand upon ideas that you've  had or just to let go of random thoughts  and start your day off with a blank  slate i think of it as like a shower for  your brain this allows you to sift  through your thoughts so that you can be  more focused and more creative  throughout the day and personally for me  i have done this with things that kind  of bother me without going into  ruminating because that can also be  another thing in and of its own because  it allows me an opportunity to really  ask myself deeper questions of why did  this thing bother me what does this say  about me and really expand upon that and  not only understand the other person but  understand myself so it can also be  really healing while also having that  extra benefit that it really can improve  your creativity greatly number three is  both simple and powerful and that is to  do one thing differently each day what i  mean here is that if you always go to  the same restaurant order the same food  sit at the same desk talk with the same  people brush your teeth with the same  hand do things differently force  yourself to sit at a different spot than  you usually used to go through a  different route than you're usually used  to or explore a different part of that  menu that you've never tried the point  of this is to fire neural connections  and get yourself out of that autopilot  mode that you've been stuck in this  allows you with the opportunity to bring  yourself to the present because it's out  of the norm your brain is now paying  attention because this is not what it's  used to doing and just doing these  simple things differently will allow you  to take ownership of your day number  four is to try a new hobby or learn a  new skill this could be something like  taking dance lessons taking a cake  decorating class or even something that  can be completely free like having a  friend teach you how to use construction  tools or learning a new language as you  gain more experiences and learn new  skills not only will you boost your  creative energy but it will also help  you improve your confidence and this  alone will go a long way towards  increasing your motivation number five  is immensely important and that is to  read books or listen to audiobooks i did  mention that you should limit media  consumption as much as possible but one  of my favorite things to do on idle time  which is that time when you're doing  something mindlessly like washing the  dishes for example is to listen to  audiobooks this allows me a time to  focus on learning and processing new  information i have several videos on the  topic of reading and its importance  which i can link down below but what i  have found that works best for me is to  use audiobooks when i'm doing things  that don't really require much thought  like cleaning the house for example and  then reading a physical book before  going to bed some people prefer to read  in the morning and that's perfectly fine  too just find what works best for you  but in any case reading is like gold  when it comes to developing  life-changing habits and boosting  creative thinking number six is to spend  time with positive or inspiring people  if you're like me from a few years back  and your conversations looked like this  hey so i got this great idea of starting  the youtube channel why would you do  that you know growing a youtube channel  is so hard these days it is so saturated  and you don't even have social media how  is it going to grow you're just  basically going to be working for free  for years i wouldn't bother if every  time you think of a new idea or decide  to try something different the people  around you only bring up the negative  points it may be time to get some more  positive influences  number seven is to watch your health i  recently shared with you my experience  with the keto diet but eliminate sugars  and processed foods from your diet okay  i know what you may be thinking what the  heck does my diet have to do with  creative thinking everything the food  that you eat directly impacts your  hormone balance your mood your physical  energy your sleep your health in general  if you physically feel crappy it's gonna  be pretty darn hard to do mundane tasks  let alone creative projects so  prioritize your health this is a must  number eight don't be so serious  make time to play and laugh science has  shown that the physiological effect of  smiling actually makes us happy through  the release of endorphins happy hormones  they reduce stress can boost your mood  and can in turn help you access that  creative power within you i love the  quote by james altucher in his book  reinvent yourself today i will try again  and tomorrow and then the next day if i  don't get better i will at least have  fun trying and what else is there in  life but to play as much as possible  number nine is one of my absolute  favorites is to spend time in nature if  you live in a very populated city you  will know that people are often in a  rush aggressive drivers are never in  shortage and the atmosphere is just go  go go my husband and i personally love  hiking and being out in nature and we  actually crave it when we've been in the  city a little more than we would like  because nature is just healing we get so  used to reacting to buzzes and beeps and  lights all day long that we become  desensitized to our surroundings and we  lose the ability to be still be present  and be in the moment to really take  things in like seeing a butterfly on a  bush  a squirrel passing by or feeling how  small we are on this huge earth when we  see a beautiful landscape spending some  time in nature will no doubt help you  slow down the pace so that you can focus  on living rather than doing and lastly  number 10 travel even remotely traveling  doesn't have to mean that you have to  pack up a suitcase and go across the  country it can be as simple as a weekend  road trip to visit nearby states or  taking the afternoon to visit a town  that you haven't explored whatever the  case may be return to your childlike  self again and find the explorer within  you that's it for today's video i hope  that you found it helpful and please  don't forget to give it a thumbs up and  subscribe for more videos on all things  living a simpler happier healthier life  thanks so much for watching until next  time  [Music]  you
 

